# TypeScript

- `strict` mode; no `any` unless at a true boundary (then narrow immediately)
- Prefer `unknown` + type guards over `any`
- Export types from models; use `z.infer<typeof Schema>` for schema-backed types
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes extended by features; `type` for unions/intersections
- Async functions always typed return (`Promise<Verdict>`, not implicit)
- Use discriminated unions for status/recommendation flows

```typescript
// ✅
type Recommendation = "approve" | "reject" | "needs_more_info";

interface Verdict {
  recommendation: Recommendation;
  confirmed: Finding[];
  unconfirmed: Finding[];
}
```

- Prefer early returns over deep nesting
- Do not use `enum`; use `as const` objects or string unions
